cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Replay Pack (.rpk) and Replay Phantom (.rph) Specifications: open formats for replayable Monte-Carlo diffusion-MRI"
message: "If you implement, emit, or consume Replay Packs or Replay Phantoms, please cite this specification."
type: standard
version: 0.3.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21692505
date-released: 2026-07-31
abstract: >
  A portable, code-free file format and replay model that stores the state of a
  Monte-Carlo random walk through a diffusion-MRI substrate so the measured signal can
  be reconstructed ("replayed") for arbitrary gradient waveforms, field strengths,
  orientations, relaxation times, surface relaxivity, and magnetization-transfer
  settings without re-running the walk. The format is independent of any compression
  scheme and supports partial ("tiered") producers, enabling interoperability across
  simulators and a shared substrate bank. A companion format, the Replay Phantom
  (.rph), composes solved packs into a voxel grid — per-voxel substrate fractions,
  proton densities, and orientation distributions in a normatively specified
  spherical-harmonic basis — holding references rather than walkers, so one solved
  substrate serves every voxel that cites it. A phantom adds no capability of its
  own: its replayable tier is the intersection of its packs'.
authors:
  - family-names: Fick
    given-names: Rutger H. J.
    affiliation: dmrai-lab
keywords:
  - diffusion MRI
  - Monte-Carlo simulation
  - microstructure
